---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import MedicalDisclaimer from '../../components/MedicalDisclaimer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead 
			title="Podcast: BMS Sufferer — Guest Guide & Interview Questions | Decoding The Burn" 
			description="Guest interview guide and format for the Decoding the Burning Mouth Syndrome Podcast. Dedicated to advancing scientific research and discovering real solutions." 
		/>
		<!-- Strictly non-indexed guest reference page -->
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="guest-guide-container">
			<div class="disclaimer-wrap">
				<MedicalDisclaimer />
			</div>

			<header class="guide-hero">
				<h1 class="guide-title">Podcast: BMS Sufferer — Guest Guide & Format</h1>
				<p class="guide-subtitle">
					Everything you need to know about joining Denis Ethier on the podcast. A relaxed, patient-led conversation designed to gather qualitative data and advance research on Burning Mouth&nbsp;Syndrome.
				</p>
			</header>

			<!-- 1. How It Works -->
			<section class="guide-section">
				<h2 class="section-title">How It Works</h2>
				<div class="steps-grid">
					<div class="step-card">
						<span class="step-number">01</span>
						<h3 class="step-heading">Relaxed & Friendly</h3>
						<p class="step-text">
							This is an informal, 30 to 45 minute video call over Riverside or Zoom. No complicated equipment or technical expertise required.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="step-card">
						<span class="step-number">02</span>
						<h3 class="step-heading">Your Story, Your Pace</h3>
						<p class="step-text">
							You only share what you are comfortable sharing. You are welcome to use your real name, first name only, or a pseudonym if you prefer privacy.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="step-card">
						<span class="step-number">03</span>
						<h3 class="step-heading">Advancing Research</h3>
						<p class="step-text">
							Each interview is published on YouTube and podcast platforms to help fellow sufferers and provide anonymized qualitative patterns for medical researchers.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- 2. Patient Interview Questions -->
			<section class="guide-section questions-section">
				<h2 class="section-title">Core Interview Questions for BMS Sufferers</h2>
				<p class="section-intro">
					During the conversation, we will explore your timeline like a detective. Here are the core topics and questions we will walk through together:
				</p>

				<div class="questions-list">
					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">1</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Onset & Initial Event</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">When did your BMS symptoms first start? What was happening in your life, health, or dental care when it began?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">2</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Progression & Timeline</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">Did the burning arrive suddenly and stay permanently, or did it start coming on and off intermittently before progressing into daily pain?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">3</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Pain Consistency & Fluctuation</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">Is your BMS pain consistent throughout the day? Is it a steady 10/10, or does it fluctuate (e.g., 5/10 in the morning, 12/10 at night, or spike after meals)?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">4</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Location & Sensations</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">Where in your mouth does the fire burn the most (tip of tongue, sides, palate, gums, inner cheeks, lips, throat)? Do you experience metallic tastes or dry mouth?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">5</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Dental History & Precursors</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">What dental procedures, crowns, fillings, root canals, or cleanings happened right before or around the time your burning began?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">6</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Daily Diet & Food Triggers</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">What does a typical day of eating and drinking look like? Have you noticed specific food triggers (coffee, wine, spices, acidic fruits, toothpastes) that add fuel to the fire?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">7</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">The Medical Gauntlet</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">How many dentists, doctors, or specialists have you consulted? What treatments, rinses, or medications were prescribed, and what happened?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">8</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Self-Experiments & Relief</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">What have you tested on your own (supplements, elimination diets, fasting, mouth taping)? Has anything provided even partial relief?</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="question-item">
						<span class="q-num">9</span>
						<div class="q-content">
							<h3 class="q-title">Your Message to Researchers</h3>
							<p class="q-desc">If you could speak directly to top medical and dental researchers, what is the single most important thing you want them to understand about living with BMS?</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- 3. Dentists, Doctors & Researchers Formats -->
			<section class="guide-section">
				<h2 class="section-title">Interview Formats for Professionals & Researchers</h2>
				<div class="pro-grid">
					<div class="pro-card">
						<div class="pro-icon" aria-hidden="true">🦷</div>
						<h3 class="pro-heading">For Dentists & Periodontists</h3>
						<p class="pro-desc">
							We discuss cervical margin integrity, hidden subgingival decay beneath crowns, exposed root dentin tubules, galvanism, and bacterial biofilm pathways that trigger trigeminal nerve sensitization.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="pro-card">
						<div class="pro-icon" aria-hidden="true">🩺</div>
						<h3 class="pro-heading">For Physicians & Neurologists</h3>
						<p class="pro-desc">
							We explore small-fiber neuropathies, autonomic dysfunction, trigeminal sensory pathways, ion channel modulation (ASIC1/ASIC3, TRPV1), and why systemic pharmaceuticals often fail to solve local oral triggers.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="pro-card">
						<div class="pro-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔬</div>
						<h3 class="pro-heading">For Academic & Literature Researchers</h3>
						<p class="pro-desc">
							We review clinical trial design, salivary biomarkers, mucosal barrier permeability, dietary elimination protocols, and methods for bridging patient-led data with formal research institutions.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CTA Box -->
			<section class="guide-cta-box">
				<h2 class="cta-title">Ready to Share Your Story?</h2>
				<p class="cta-subtitle">
					Join Denis on the podcast to help decode this condition and ensure no one navigates this fire in&nbsp;silence.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-actions">
					<a href="/podcast#apply" class="btn btn-primary cta-btn">Apply to Be a Guest &rarr;</a>
					<a href="/podcast" class="btn btn-outline cta-btn">Back to Podcast Hub</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />

		<style>
			.guest-guide-container {
				max-width: 860px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 6rem 1.5rem;
			}

			.disclaimer-wrap {
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.guide-hero {
				text-align: center;
				margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
			}

			.guide-title {
				font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem);
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				letter-spacing: -0.025em;
				line-height: 1.18;
				margin: 0 auto 1.25rem auto;
				text-wrap: balance;
			}

			.guide-subtitle {
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
				color: #334155;
				max-width: 700px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				text-wrap: balance;
			}

			.guide-section {
				margin-bottom: 4rem;
			}

			.section-title {
				font-size: 1.75rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
			}

			.section-intro {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
				color: #475569;
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.steps-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.25rem;
			}

			.step-card {
				background: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
				border-radius: 14px;
				padding: 1.75rem;
				box-shadow: 0 4px 16px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
			}

			.step-number {
				display: inline-block;
				font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
				font-size: 0.82rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #be123c;
				background: #fff1f2;
				border: 1px solid #fecdd3;
				padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
				border-radius: 6px;
				margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
			}

			.step-heading {
				font-size: 1.18rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
			}

			.step-text {
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
				color: #475569;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.questions-list {
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				gap: 1rem;
			}

			.question-item {
				display: flex;
				align-items: flex-start;
				gap: 1.25rem;
				background: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
				border-radius: 12px;
				padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem;
				box-shadow: 0 2px 8px -2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);
				transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
			}

			.question-item:hover {
				border-color: #cbd5e1;
				transform: translateX(3px);
			}

			.q-num {
				flex-shrink: 0;
				width: 32px;
				height: 32px;
				background: #be123c;
				color: #ffffff;
				border-radius: 50%;
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				font-weight: 800;
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				margin-top: 0.1rem;
			}

			.q-content {
				flex: 1;
			}

			.q-title {
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 0.35rem 0;
			}

			.q-desc {
				font-size: 0.96rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
				color: #475569;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.pro-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.25rem;
			}

			.pro-card {
				background: #f8fafc;
				border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
				border-radius: 14px;
				padding: 1.75rem;
			}

			.pro-icon {
				font-size: 1.85rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
			}

			.pro-heading {
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
			}

			.pro-desc {
				font-size: 0.92rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
				color: #475569;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.guide-cta-box {
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, #faf5ff 0%, #f5f3ff 100%);
				border: 1px solid #e9d5ff;
				border-left: 5px solid #7c3aed;
				border-radius: 18px;
				padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
				text-align: center;
				margin-top: 3.5rem;
			}

			.cta-title {
				font-size: 1.65rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				margin: 0 0 0.65rem 0;
			}

			.cta-subtitle {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
				color: #475569;
				max-width: 600px;
				margin: 0 auto 1.75rem auto;
				text-wrap: balance;
			}

			.cta-actions {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: center;
				gap: 1rem;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
			}

			.cta-btn {
				padding: 0.75rem 1.65rem;
				font-weight: 700;
				text-decoration: none;
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
